<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initialscale=1.0" /><meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge" /><style type="text/css">@media screen and (max-width: 480px) {
  .contentbuilderBaseColumnRow .columnCell {display:inline-block; width:100%}
}
 .contentpageDefaultEmailTemplatePageTemplate .contentRoot {width:600px}
@media only screen and (max-width: 480px) {
  .contentpageDefaultEmailTemplatePageTemplate .contentRoot {width:320px}
}
 </style></head><body><table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" class="contentpageDefaultEmailTemplatePageTemplate" id="contentpage_emailTemplateBodyContent" style="background-color:#E9EAEC;"><tr><td width="100%" align="center"><table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" role="presentation" class="contentRoot"><tr><td style="padding-right:10px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-top:10px;padding-left:10px;"><table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="contentbuilderBaseColumnRow" role="presentation" bgcolor=""><tr valign="top"><td class="columnCell" style="vertical-align:top;" width="100%"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;word-break:break-word;" role="presentation" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" locked="0"><tr><td style="" align="Center"><img style="max-width:100%;width:100%;display:block;border:none;" width="600" src="https://storage.pardot.com/492991/1606233699clLqzSUI/WelcomeMemberRenewal_Header.jpg" alt="" /></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="contentbuilderBaseColumnRow" role="presentation" bgcolor=""><tr valign="top"><td class="columnCell" style="vertical-align:top;" width="100%"><table style="font-size:14px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;word-break:break-word;" role="presentation" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" locked="0"><tr><td style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="line-height:107%"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif">Dear {{{Recipient.FirstName}}},</span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="line-height:107%"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:11.5pt"><span style="line-height:107%">Thank you for your continued membership and engagement in IACMI – The Composites Institute. While 2020 has been a challenging year for the composites industry and the entire world, your participation has helped sustain IACMI as a national driver for improving manufacturing competitiveness. We were able to convene our members twice for members meetings, once in person and once virtually, providing unique opportunities for attendees to connect and network, as well as learn. Technical project work has continued, albeit slowed by the pandemic, and IACMI member companies and core partners stepped up to provide critical PPE and other health and safety solutions to combat the crisis, showing the resilience of the composites industry.<br />
<br />
In December, you will receive an invoice for your 2021 membership fees, which will be due in January. Over the course of 2020, IACMI has issued pro-rated invoices from your normal renewal date through December 2020. This was done to shift and harmonize all member renewals to occur at the beginning of each calendar year moving forward. The 2021 invoice, once paid, will continue your IACMI membership through December 2021.</span></span></span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">As an IACMI Consortium Member, you have direct access to expertise and key decision makers across the composites industry through strategic planning meetings, roadmapping events, and technical project collaborations. IACMI provides members the opportunity to connect face-to-face with the entire supply chain through exclusive networking events, including Members Meetings and partner events. Additional member-only benefits include: </span></span></span>
<ul style="list-style-type:square">
	<li class="Default"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">Access to world class innovation spaces and resources across the U.S., including accredited technician training and workforce development programs.</span></span></span></span></li>
	<li class="Default"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">Participation in focused working groups and access to leverage equipment and facility investments of over $250 million.</span></span></span></span></li>
	<li class="Default"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">Exposure to new markets and connections through IACMI and/or IACMI media partner communication channels.</span></span></span></span></li>
	<li class="Default"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">Opportunities to participate in IACMI Consortium governance (seats voted on by members) through the Consortium Council, providing strategic direction for IACMI and influencing future investments.</span></span></span></span></li>
</ul>
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">Your member fees are used to manage the IACMI Consortium and cover the costs of Members Meetings, presence at other industry meetings and events, and communications. New for 2021, a portion of member fees will go toward the creation of a Resource Pool to fund R&amp;D projects and other activities proposed by the membership. Any members stepping up to IACMI Premium membership ($50,000 annually) will automatically receive a seat on the Consortium Council and a minimum of 50% of your membership fees will go to the Resource Pool. Please contact me if interested in this opportunity for increased influence on the direction of IACMI.</span></span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">As we enter 2021, we are already hard at work developing programming for our virtual Members Meeting February 16-18 and an in-person Members Meeting in Detroit, Michigan July 20-22 (conditions permitting). Look for the formation of additional working groups and other opportunities to engage with IACMI and fellow members.</span></span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">We are excited to work with you to make 2021 a year of continued impact for you and the industry. We appreciate your ongoing support of IACMI - The Composites Institute and look forward to future collaboration as a collective voice to accelerate the adoption of advanced composites.</span></span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-size:11.5pt">Best wishes for the holiday season,</span></span></span></span><br />
&nbsp;</td></tr></table></td></tr></table><table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="contentbuilderBaseColumnRow" role="presentation" bgcolor=""><tr valign="top"><td class="columnCell" style="vertical-align:top;" width="100%"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;word-break:break-word;" role="presentation" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" locked="0"><tr><td style="" align="left"><img style="max-width:25%;width:100%;display:block;border:none;" width="150" src="https://storage.pardot.com/492991/1606233532RzYNhlqU/Dale_sig.jpg" alt="" /></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="contentbuilderBaseColumnRow" role="presentation" bgcolor=""><tr valign="top"><td class="columnCell" style="vertical-align:top;" width="100%"><table style="font-size:14px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;word-break:break-word;" role="presentation" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" locked="0"><tr><td style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><b>Dale Brosius&nbsp;</b><br />
Chief Commercialization Officer &amp;<br />
IACMI Consortium Executive Director</td></tr></table></td></tr></table><table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="contentbuilderBaseColumnRow" role="presentation" bgcolor=""><tr valign="top"><td class="columnCell" style="vertical-align:top;" width="100%"><table style="font-size:14px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;word-break:break-word;" role="presentation" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" locked="0"><tr><td style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><p style="text-align: center;"><b><span style="line-height:1;">IACMI - The Composites Institute</span></b></p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="line-height:1;">2360 Cherahala Blvd.</span></p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="line-height:1;">Knoxville, TN 37932</span></p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="{{{EmailPreferenceCenter}}}">Email preferences</a> | <a href="{{{Unsubscribe}}}">Unsubscribe</a><br />
<br />
&nbsp;</p></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></body></html>